{"created": "2026-11-18T05:36:19.862858+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-18T05:48:46.427390+00:00", "id": 24331415, "conceptrecid": "24331414", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24331415", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.24331414", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24331415", "metadata": {"title": "Code and data for \"Lyapunov Certification as Max-Plus Inference: Exact Decomposition, Scalable Synthesis, and Rigorous Region-of-Attraction Certificates for Large Nonlinear Networks\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24331415", "publication_date": "2026-11-18", "description": "<p>Software, run settings and complete result files for the paper \"Lyapunov Certification as Max-Plus Inference: Exact Decomposition, Scalable Synthesis, and Rigorous Region-of-Attraction Certificates for Large Nonlinear Networks\" by Yuan Shen (submitted to IEEE Transactions on Automatic Control).</p>\n<p>The method writes the Lyapunov inequalities of a network as local inequalities that are coupled by max-plus messages on a junction tree. A sparse LP inside a counterexample-guided loop (structured interior-point method) synthesizes the certificate. An outward-rounded interval Taylor branch-and-bound with a C kernel verifies it bag by bag. A Krawczyk enclosure of the equilibrium closes the argument, and an independent pure-Python implementation re-verifies the certificate.</p>\n<p>Contents:<br>- code/: Python modules, the C interval kernel, one script per experiment, and the driver script (code/tools/rerun_round2.sh) that produced every result.<br>- results/round2/: every result file behind the numbers, tables and figures of the paper and its Supplementary Material: logs, JSON records, exported certificates, independent re-verifications and the record of the computing environment.<br>- feeders/: OpenDSS files of the IEEE 123-bus and 8500-node test feeders, and the network graphs derived from them.<br>- paper/ and notes/: the generated LaTeX macros that hold every number of the paper, and the source file and field of each number.</p>\n<p>Reproduction: README.md covers the following:<br>- the environment;<br>- quick checks: the number scripts regenerate the shipped macro files byte for byte from the shipped results;<br>- self-tests;<br>- the full re-run (12.5 h on a 64-core server);<br>- a table that maps each table and figure of the paper to its jobs and result files.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Shen, Yuan", "affiliation": "University of British Columbia, Okanagan Campus"}], "keywords": ["Lyapunov methods", "region of attraction", "large-scale systems", "sparsity", "max-plus algebra", "interval analysis", "power system stability", "grid-forming inverters", "junction tree", "interval Taylor models", "counterexample-guided synthesis"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.24331675", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "v1", "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "24331414"}}]}}, "title": "Code and data for \"Lyapunov Certification as Max-Plus Inference: Exact Decomposition, Scalable Synthesis, and Rigorous Region-of-Attraction Certificates for Large Nonlinear Networks\"", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24331415", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24331415", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24331415?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24331415", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24331415", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.24331415", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24331415/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24331414", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24331414", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24331414", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.24331414", "se